cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  MeSH Workbench: MeSH co-occurrence concept networks for
  Adverse Outcome Pathways
message: >-
  If you use this software or the networks it produces in
  published work, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sax
    given-names: Jakob
    email: jakob.sax@ki.se
    affiliation: Karolinska Institutet
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Tox-pub/Mesh-Network-Analysis'
abstract: >-
  Builds and validates MeSH co-occurrence concept networks
  from the PubMed literature, connecting chemical stressors
  to adverse outcomes through biological intermediates in
  the shape of an Adverse Outcome Pathway. Retrieval is
  date-chunked over NCBI E-utilities and expanded across
  citation generations; the co-occurrence graph is filtered
  by a consensus of generalised local filtering and
  simulated annealing; nodes are scored by a Mean Relevancy
  Score over the whole indexed corpus. Ships as a desktop
  application carrying its own Python for Windows, Linux and
  macOS, and as a command-line pipeline. Includes a PRISMA
  flow report, a run ledger, and benchmarking against a
  curated ground-truth set.
keywords:
  - MeSH
  - adverse outcome pathway
  - text mining
  - co-occurrence network
  - PubMed
  - toxicology
  - skin sensitisation
license: MIT
version: 3.2.0
